---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import TopologyScene from '../components/TopologyScene.astro';

const capabilities = [
  ['Native Wayland terminal', 'Implemented'],
  ['Persistent sessions', 'Validated'],
  ['Panes, tabs, and restore', 'Validated'],
  ['Bounded automation', 'Validated'],
  ['Public distribution', 'Not released'],
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Splinterm — persistent terminal sessions, bounded automation"
  description="Splinterm is a persistent, security-conscious terminal substrate for humans and bounded automation."
>
  <section class="hero shell-section">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <img class="hero-mark" src="/favicon.svg" alt="" width="112" height="112" />
      <p class="eyebrow"><span>Advanced private prerelease</span> · Enter the Lair</p>
      <h1>Your shell should outlive its <em>window.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        Splinterm keeps your work below the surface: Lairs hold projects, Dojos hold working
        sessions, and Splints keep their shells alive when graphical clients disappear.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Read the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/status/">See what works today</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">Built in Rust from Foot’s terminal behavior. Quietly disciplined for Omarchy.</p>
    </div>
    <TopologyScene />
  </section>

  <section class="manifesto shell-section" aria-labelledby="persistence-title">
    <div class="section-index" aria-hidden="true">01 / Below the surface</div>
    <div class="manifesto-copy">
      <h2 id="persistence-title">The work lives in the Lair.<br />Windows only visit.</h2>
      <p>
        <code>splinterd</code> keeps the topology underground. A Lair gathers the work, each Dojo
        holds a focused session, and every Splint carries a running shell. Windows are temporary views in.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="sequence" aria-label="Persistent session workflow">
      <li><span>01</span><strong>Enter</strong><small>Open a Lair and gather the work.</small></li>
      <li><span>02</span><strong>Train</strong><small>Shape a Dojo from tabs, panes, and Splints.</small></li>
      <li><span>03</span><strong>Return</strong><small>Leave the window; find the same Dojo later.</small></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="control-section shell-section" aria-labelledby="control-title">
    <div class="section-index" aria-hidden="true">02 / Shared substrate</div>
    <div class="control-heading">
      <h2 id="control-title">One Lair.<br />Two deliberate ways in.</h2>
      <p>Human hands and bounded automation can enter the same topology without inheriting the same authority.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="control-grid">
      <article class="control-card human-card">
        <div class="card-label"><span>Human</span><i>native client</i></div>
        <h3>Hands on the Dojo</h3>
        <p>Wayland windows, tabs, panes, search, clipboard, and explicit control transfer.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Trusted application chrome</li>
          <li>Native session picker</li>
          <li>Visible authority state</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="control-card automation-card">
        <div class="card-label"><span>Automation</span><i>bounded client</i></div>
        <h3>Allowed in, never unleashed</h3>
        <p>JSON/NDJSON, an SSH stdio relay, and MCP—always subject to explicit policy.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Exact executable identity</li>
          <li>Resource and scope limits</li>
          <li>Revocable controller leases</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="boundary-note"><span aria-hidden="true">◆</span> Discipline is structural: terminal output remains data, never authority or automatic instruction.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="status-section shell-section" aria-labelledby="status-title">
    <div class="section-index" aria-hidden="true">03 / Current state</div>
    <div class="status-intro">
      <h2 id="status-title">Forged in private.<br />Not ready for daylight.</h2>
      <p>
        Splinterm is an advanced private prerelease. Core terminal, persistence, multiplexing,
        graphical, packaging, and automation paths exist; public support guarantees do not.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/status/">Read the complete status and limits <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-list">
      {capabilities.map(([name, status], index) => (
        <div class="capability-row">
          <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <strong>{name}</strong>
          <i class:list={{ pending: status === 'Not released' }}>{status}</i>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="first-workflow shell-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The ordinary path into the Lair</p>
      <h2 id="workflow-title">Leave the window.<br />Return to the Dojo.</h2>
      <p>Install the current private package, open a Splint, then use the session picker whenever you want the running work back.</p>
      <a class="button primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Follow the local quickstart</a>
    </div>
    <div class="command-stack" aria-label="Example Splinterm commands">
      <div><span>$</span><code>./install.sh</code></div>
      <div><span>$</span><code>splinterm sessions</code><small>choose a running Dojo</small></div>
      <div><span>$</span><code>splinterm reopen</code><small>return to the last one</small></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-gateway shell-section" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Know the passages</p>
      <h2 id="docs-title">Go as deep as the work requires.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="gateway-links">
      <a href="/docs/quickstart/"><span>Start using Splinterm</span><small>Install, launch, detach, and return.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/configure/configuration/"><span>Configure the terminal</span><small>Fonts, sizing, theme, panes, and migration.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/sessions/"><span>Understand persistence</span><small>Lairs, Dojos, Splints, windows, and lifecycle.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/development/"><span>Develop and contribute</span><small>Workspace structure, checks, and architecture.</small><i>↗</i></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
